What this is
  Written in Go.
  3 modules (folders of code), holding 9 named pieces of code such as
  functions and types.
  Serves no HTTP endpoint enola could find. enola found no database or other
  data store.
  enola recognised no common way of organising the folders. (likely)

Structure: needs attention
  1 circular dependency: modules that depend on each other in a loop, so none
  of them can be changed or tested on its own.

Start reading here
  main  (main.go:10)
    The program starts here. From here the code reaches 3 functions in 3
    modules.

Careful when changing
  No module stands out: a change in one part of the code stays fairly local.
  (likely)

Worth a look (most certain first)
  2 functions look unused. Check each one before deleting it: code outside
  this repository, or code called by name at runtime, may still use it.
  (likely)

Take with a grain of salt
  Unused code is found by matching names. Code reached through reflection,
  configuration or another repository can look unused when it is not.
  enola reads the code and never runs it: it reports structure, not behaviour
  or speed.

